The owner reports recurring flickering, blinking, or disappearing geometry in Engineering.

These defects must be investigated and repaired.

DO NOT assume that every flickering surface is caused by Z-fighting.

Possible sources include:

- Coplanar duplicate faces.
- Overlapping geometric panels.
- Duplicate floor meshes.
- Intersecting wall trim surfaces.
- Poor monitor plane placement.
- Shadow acne.
- Incorrect shadow bias.
- Depth-buffer precision.
- Transparent material sorting.
- Texture aliasing or shimmer.
- Unintended repeated object mounting.
- Camera-dependent cutaway visibility logic.
- Unstable material or geometry state.

Investigate the actual affected objects.

Do not claim root cause without evidence.

